              "text": "prēlum, prēlī — \"a press (for wine or oil)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Servī ūvās in prēlō premunt. The slaves press the grapes in the press."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Second declension, neuter: prēlum, prēlī n., also praelum. The heavy beam that squeezed grapes and olives."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "prēlum is built on premō 'to press' (EtymDB; Lewis & Short), from an older prem-lom. English press comes from the same verb."
