          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "īnserō, īnserere — \"to graft, to plant in\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Agricola rāmum pirī in mālum īnserit. The farmer grafts a pear branch onto an apple tree."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "īnserō, īnserere, īnsēvī, īnsitum, from serō, serere, sēvī 'to sow'. A different verb īnserō, īnserere, īnseruī, īnsertum 'to put in' gives English insert."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "īnserō 'to graft' is built from in- 'in' and serō, serere, sēvī 'to sow, to plant' (EtymDB; Lewis & Short). It must be kept apart from īnserō 'to put in', from serō, seruī 'to join'."
            }
          ]
        },
