              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "vindēmia, vindēmiae — \"the grape harvest, the vintage\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Autumnō vindēmia est; tōta familia ūvās legit. In autumn it is the grape harvest; the whole household gathers grapes."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "First declension, feminine: vindēmia, vindēmiae f. English vintage comes from it through French."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "vindēmia is built from vīnum 'wine, grapes' and dēmō 'to take off, to remove' (EtymDB; Lewis & Short): taking the grapes off the vine. English vintage comes from it through French."
            }
          ]
        },
